---
title: Steak au Poivre
cooklang: 2
servings: 2
cuisine: French
source: recipe-pack dinner-8/7032-steak-au-poivre-2
---

= Steaks -> rested steaks

`Pat` @sirloin steaks{2}(2.5 cm thick) dry with #paper towels{} on a #board{} and `season` both
sides with @salt{1%tsp}.

`Press` @black peppercorns{1%tbsp}(coarsely crushed) onto the @&sirloin steaks{} to form a crust.
-> seasoned steaks

`Heat medium-high` @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @unsalted butter{15%g} in a #frying pan{} over medium-high heat.

`Sear` the @&seasoned steaks{} in the #&frying pan{} for ~{2-3%minutes} per side for medium-rare.

`Remove` the @&seasoned steaks{} to a #plate{} and `rest covered` them loosely covered with #foil{}.

= Peppercorn sauce -> sauce

`Melt medium` @&unsalted butter{15%g} in the #&frying pan{} over medium heat.

`Sauté` @shallot{1}(finely chopped) and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) for ~{1%minute} until ~{fragrant}.

`Stir in` @Dijon mustard{1%tsp} and @Worcestershire sauce{1%tbsp}.

`Deglaze` with @brandy{60%ml} and `reduce` for ~{1%minute}.

`Pour in` @beef stock{120%ml} and @heavy cream{120%ml}, stirring until ~{thickened}.

`Season` with @&salt{1/2%tsp} and @?crushed black peppercorns{1/2%tsp}(for extra heat) and
`simmer` for ~{2%minutes}.

= Serve

`Return` the @&rested steaks{} to the #&frying pan{} and `spoon` the @&sauce{} over them.
`Serve` immediately with @?mashed potatoes{}.
